# Keep line endings sane across machines.
#
# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository and given the platform's
# own endings on checkout, which is the default and is fine for everything
# here EXCEPT the Windows launchers below.
* text=auto

# These are read by cmd.exe and the Windows Script Host, both of which are
# genuinely fussy about line endings -- a .bat checked out with bare LF can
# misparse labels and multi-line blocks. They are Windows-only files by
# nature, so they are pinned to CRLF wherever they are checked out.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary, so git never tries to "fix" them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.aseprite binary
